course: dictionary
lesson: 8195
title: Restorers and the words that help us know them
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A restorer is a person whose job is to repair old things, such as paintings, furniture, buildings or objects, so they look as they used to. You can spot the job in the word itself: restore means bring back, and -er often means a person who does something.
explain: «A clear varnish protects an oil painting, but it yellows over time; restorers, experts who carefully clean old art, can reveal bright colours under old varnish and dirt.» The words «experts who carefully clean old art» are the context clues. They tell you what a restorer does, even if you have never met the word before.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «experts who carefully clean old art» still make sense in place of «restorers»? Yes, so you are on the right track. Sometimes the clue is a little further away, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A restorer is a person whose job is to repair old paintings, furniture, buildings or objects.
fact: To restore something means to bring it back to how it used to look.
fact: In «restorers, experts who carefully clean old art», the clue words show that restorers are careful experts.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «furniture restorer» and «art restorer».
fact: A restorer can also be a product, such as hair restorer, which restores something.
exercise: «Restorers, experts who carefully clean old art, can reveal bright colours under old varnish and dirt.» What is a restorer? | A person who paints new pictures to sell in shops | *A person who repairs old paintings and objects so they look as they used to | A machine that makes paint dry faster | A museum guard who watches the visitors
exercise: Mum takes an old wooden chair to a furniture restorer. Why? | So the chair can be sold as a new chair | *So the chair can be repaired and look as it used to | So the chair can be painted by the children | So the chair can be used as a ladder
exercise: Hair restorer is a phrase. What kind of thing is a hair restorer? | A dog that lives in a salon | A kind of hairbrush | A person who cuts hair | *A product that restores something
test: Which phrase names a person who repairs old paintings? | art shop | furniture box | *art restorer | hair restorer
test: In «restorers ... can reveal bright colours under old varnish and dirt», what do restorers do to the old varnish and dirt? | Make them yellow on purpose | Leave them alone for ever | *Clean them away carefully to show the colours underneath | Paint over them in red
exam: What does «restorer» mean? | A painter who only makes new pictures | *A person or product that brings something back to how it used to look | A room in a museum where paintings are sold | A tool for cutting paper
